From 75ceef276e6e8de4018e87d4b202f088a43756a7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 11:26:13 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] delta responses: flush a held start before pathsend,
 Vary + no ETag on a delta, one origin per scope

Follow-up to #2024: the three non-blocking nits of its approving review
(https://github.com/example-org/hermes/pull/2024#pullrequestreview-5889450333).

1. Gateway, `_DeltaSend`: an eligible `http.response.start` is held until the body is complete. Any other message
   (`http.response.pathsend`, `http.response.zerocopysend`: the server sends the file itself) was forwarded while
   the start was still held, so the start never went out. Now the held start goes out first, unchanged, followed
   by any body collected so far, then the message; the rest of that response passes through. Latent today
   (uvicorn does not advertise pathsend, web_server.py has no FileResponse).

2. Gateway, hashed and delta answers: `Vary: X-Hermes-Delta-Accept, X-Hermes-Delta-Base`, merged into the
   handler's own Vary as one header (names kept once, `*` left alone). A delta also drops the handler's `ETag`:
   its bytes are a zstd frame, not the entity that validator names. A whole hashed body keeps its ETag (the bytes
   are the handler's). A caching proxy in front of the gateway (a Cloudflare-published one) can then not replay a
   delta to a client that did not ask. Unasked and un-encoded answers keep exactly the handler's headers.

3. Desktop, `DeltaBodyStore.bindRemote`: one origin per scope. Binding a scope to a new origin drops its earlier
   origin, so a tunnel rebuilt on a new local port without `stopPoolBackend` no longer leaves the old port asked
   for deltas or able to file answers under the scope. The scope's copies are kept and follow it to the new
   origin: that is the documented tunnel-rebuild case ("survives a tunnel rebuild" test, unchanged).

Tests (RED without the source change, GREEN with it):
- tests/hermes_cli/test_web_delta_response.py: start + pathsend / zerocopysend with a delta asked yields start
  then the file message; body collected before a pathsend goes out after the start; Vary on hashed and delta
  answers, merged with a handler's two Vary headers; ETag kept on a whole body and absent on a delta; `Vary: *`
  untouched. 34 passed (28 passed, 6 failed on the old source).
- apps/desktop/electron/delta-reads.test.ts: a rebind without a teardown stops the old port being asked or
  filed under the scope, the copy moves to the new origin, other scopes are untouched. 23 passed (1 failed on
  the old source).

One existing assertion changed on purpose: `test_other_headers_survive_a_delta_duplicates_included` asserted the
delta kept `etag == "abc"`, which is the behaviour nit 2 removes; it now asserts the whole answer has the ETag
and the delta does not. Its other assertions (cache-control, both Set-Cookie headers) are unchanged.
